	(text "Verified vs not (2026-11-17, power agent)\n\nTwo SWD targets, each on a standard 10-pin 1.27 mm Cortex header with a DNP Tag-Connect TC2030-NL alternate:\n  J3 + J34 -> nRF9151 (SWDIO_MCU / SWDCLK_MCU / RESET_MCU_N), J32 + J35 -> BT840 (SWDIO_BLE / SWDCLK_BLE / RESET_BLE_N).\n  Cortex pinout and TC2030 pinout both verified from the Tag-Connect TC2030-CTX datasheet. SWO (pin 6) unused on both.\nnRF9151 reset (nRF9151 HDG, nRESET + nRESET circuit example): 13k internal pull-up to 2.2 V, NO external pull-up allowed,\n  about 1k series (R313) + bypass cap at the pin (connectivity sheet). Nothing on RESET_MCU_N may drive it to 3.3 V.\n  SWD is available 100-500 ms after ENABLE goes high (HDG ENABLE) -- give the debugger a connect delay.\nBT840 reset: P0.18 needs UICR.PSELRESET set by BT840 firmware before SW11/J32 pin 10 reset works (NOT re-verified: nRF52840 PS blocked).\nDebug UART J33: 3.3 V logic, pin 4 isolated unless R314 fitted. No USB-UART bridge footprint (not trivial without a data USB-C).\nButtons SW2/SW11/SW12: Omron B3U-1000P (Omron B3U catalogue), footprint Button_Switch_SMD:SW_SPST_B3U-1000P."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "03a9eec9-1d06-4afa-9c19-3e445ff66452")
	)
)
